        "hasTitle" : true,
        "message" : [
          "%md\r",
          "The first cell creates and saves your cycle-clustering model.\r",
          "- cycle_input selects the account ID and three normalized cycle measures.\r",
          "- oml.km(n_clusters=5) selects Oracle’s built-in K-Means and requests five groups.\r",
          "- .fit(...) trains it on the accounts’ cycle values.\r",
          "- case_id=\"ACCOUNT_ID\" uses the account ID only to identify each account, not as a cycle measure.\r",
          "- model_name=\"BANK_CYCLE_KMEANS_MODEL\" saves the trained model in Oracle Database.\r",
          "- cycle_model is the Python name you use to access that saved model in the notebook.\r",
          "\r",
          "BANK_CYCLE_KMEANS_MODEL is trained on:\r",
          "- CYCLE_2_NORM\r",
          "- CYCLE_3_NORM\r",
          "- CYCLE_4_NORM\r",
          "ACCOUNT_ID only identifies each account.\r",
          "\r",
          "The model groups the accounts into five clusters based on those three normalized cycle measures\r",
          "\r",
          "ACCOUNT_ID tells us which account belongs to each resulting cluster"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
        "enabled" : true,
        "forms" : "[]",
        "result" : {
          "startTime" : 1787738142871,
          "endTime" : 1787738142963,
          "interpreter" : "md.medium",
          "taskStatus" : "SUCCESS",
          "status" : "SUCCESS",
          "results" : [
            {
              "message" : "<p>The first cell creates and saves your cycle-clustering model.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>cycle_input selects the account ID and three normalized cycle measures.</li>\n<li>oml.km(n_clusters=5) selects Oracle’s built-in K-Means and requests five groups.</li>\n<li>.fit(...) trains it on the accounts’ cycle values.</li>\n<li>case_id=&quot;ACCOUNT_ID&quot; uses the account ID only to identify each account, not as a cycle measure.</li>\n<li>model_name=&quot;BANK_CYCLE_KMEANS_MODEL&quot; saves the trained model in Oracle Database.</li>\n<li>cycle_model is the Python name you use to access that saved model in the notebook.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>BANK_CYCLE_KMEANS_MODEL is trained on:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>CYCLE_2_NORM</li>\n<li>CYCLE_3_NORM</li>\n<li>CYCLE_4_NORM\nACCOUNT_ID only identifies each account.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The model groups the accounts into five clusters based on those three normalized cycle measures</p>\n<p>ACCOUNT_ID tells us which account belongs to each resulting cluster</p>\n",
              "type" : "HTML"
            }
          ],
          "forms" : "[]"
        },
        "relations" : [ ],
        "dynamicFormParams" : "{}"
      },
      {
        "row" : 0,
        "col" : 0,
        "sizeX" : 0,
        "width" : 12,
        "title" : "Train and Save the Cycle-Behaviour K-Means Model (Five Clusters)",
        "hasTitle" : true,
        "message" : [
          "%python\r",
          "# It trains the model and saves it as BANK_CYCLE_KMEANS_MODEL.\r",
          "\r",
          "cycle_input = bank_features[\r",
          "    [\"ACCOUNT_ID\", \"CYCLE_2_NORM\", \"CYCLE_3_NORM\", \"CYCLE_4_NORM\"]\r",
          "]\r",
          "\r",
          "cycle_settings = {\r",
          "    \"KMNS_ITERATIONS\": 50,\r",
          "    \"KMNS_DISTANCE\": \"KMNS_EUCLIDEAN\",\r",
          "    \"KMNS_DETAILS\": \"KMNS_DETAILS_ALL\",\r",
          "    \"PREP_AUTO\": \"OFF\"\r",
          "}\r",
          "\r",
          "cycle_model = oml.km(n_clusters=5, **cycle_settings).fit(\r",
          "    cycle_input,\r",
          "    model_name=\"BANK_CYCLE_KMEANS_MODEL\",\r",
          "    case_id=\"ACCOUNT_ID\"\r",
          ")\r",
          "\r",
          "print(\"ok\")"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "raw",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : false,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
        "enabled" : true,
        "forms" : "[]",
